A Node.js interpreter that builds single executable applications
(node --build-sea) without LIEF, and so without its mbedtls dependency.

Upstream rewrites the whole executable with LIEF to add the application blob.
This port instead reserves spare program header slots when linking node and
appends the blob in place, which keeps the program header table in the first
page where FreeBSD's image activator requires it, and leaves every existing
ELF note untouched.

It installs a single interpreter, bin/node26-sea, and nothing else: it is a
build tool for producing single executable applications rather than a
replacement for www/node26, and the two can be installed side by side.
